  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "One-third of the flowers in a garden are blue. What is the ratio of the number of blue flowers to the number of other-coloured flowers?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1:2$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fraction of other-coloured flowers}&=1-\\frac{1}{3}\\\\\\text{Fraction of other-coloured flowers}&=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nDivide the flowers into $3$ equal parts. Blue flowers occupy $1$ part and other-coloured flowers occupy $2$ parts.\n\nTherefore, blue flowers : other-coloured flowers $=1:2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
